                            <h2 class="nwe-toke-txt-4 mb-3 text-center" data-aos="fade-up">
                                What is Digital <span class="curve-text">Asset</span> Tokenization?
                            </h2>
                            <p class="nw-w-txt-2 text-center mb-3" style="color: #0000008f;" data-aos="fade-up">
                                A real-world asset property, gold, equity, artwork, a fund, or a bond has value.
                                Blockchain digital asset tokenization converts this value into easily splitable,
                                tradable, and accessible by investors worldwide. Tokenization platform development is
                                the work of building the full infrastructure, including smart contracts, KYC, and the
                                compliance layer.
                            </p>
                            <p class="nw-w-txt-2 text-center mb-3" style="color: #0000008f;" data-aos="fade-up">
                                Each token represents a share or unit of value tied to a real-world or digital asset.
                                These tokens can be securely bought, sold, or transferred on a marketplace. At Clarisco,
                                our real-world asset tokenization development covers every one of these layers built to
                                your asset class, your jurisdiction, and your investor base.
                            </p>

                            <div data-aos="fade-up" class="mt-5 col-md-8 mx-auto">
                                <img loading="lazy" width="4744" height="2204" src="https://assets.clarisco.com/assets/rwa-nw/digitalassets/banner/Banner1.webp"
                                    alt="Digital Asset tokenization" class="img-fluid" />
                            </div>
                            <div class="text-center mt-4" data-aos="fade-up">
                                <button class="nwe-toke-btn-1" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#PopForm">
                                    Talk To A Tokenization Export</button>
                            </div>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
