            <% const accordionData=[ { title: "My asset is worth a lot, but only a handful of buyers can afford it" ,
                content: "We convert your assets into thousands of tradeable tokens across regions and make them accessible to investors at any budget."
                }, { title: "I want to tokenize my real estate, but I doubt legal and compliance" ,
                content: "Our team works with your legal counsel to structure the token as a compliant one and set up the KYC/AML for your jurisdiction."
                }, { title: "How can investors buy these tokens? Do they need a crypto wallet?" ,
                content: "Not necessarily. We build fiat on-ramp options into the platform so investors can purchase tokens using bank accounts or cards."
                }, { title: "What happens after the tokens are issued? Where do investors trade them?" ,
                content: "We build a secondary market module directly into the platform so token holders can buy and sell among themselves."
                }, { title: "I'm worried about smart contract bugs, one exploit, and the whole project is gone" ,
                content: "Every smart contract we write goes through independent third-party security audits before deployment."
                }, { title: "How do I pay out dividends or rental income to hundreds of token holders automatically?" ,
                content: "Smart contracts handle all distributions automatically. When income comes in, it is split proportionally across every token holder."
                }, { title: "My investors are in different countries. Can the platform handle this?" ,
                content: "Yes. We build multi-currency support, jurisdiction-specific KYC flows, and configurable compliance rules for different countries."
                }, { title: "I already have an existing platform. Can tokenization be added to it?" ,
                content: "We build tokenization as a modular layer that connects to your existing systems via API, no need to rebuild what you already have."
                } ]; %>

